---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="WhisperFlow — Your voice, finally heard."
  description="Open-source, local-first AI voice dictation. Hold a key, speak naturally, get polished text in any app — powered by whisper.cpp and llama.cpp on your machine. Free forever, unlimited, no cloud."
>
  <!-- ================= HERO — the void ================= -->
  <section class="void-glow relative overflow-hidden">
    <!-- animated voice-line -->
    <svg class="pointer-events-none absolute left-0 top-40 h-40 w-full text-[#2952E3]/50" viewBox="0 0 1440 160" fill="none" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true">
      <path class="squiggle" d="M-20 110 C 180 60, 340 150, 560 100 S 980 40, 1200 110 S 1400 140, 1460 90" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round"/>
    </svg>
    <div class="relative mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 pb-10 pt-24 text-center sm:px-6 sm:pt-36">
      <p class="mx-auto inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full border border-line bg-white/[0.03] px-4 py-1.5 font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.14em] text-ink-dim">
        <span class="h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#4C6FFF] shadow-[0_0_10px_rgba(76,111,255,0.9)]"></span>
        OPEN-SOURCE · LOCAL-FIRST · NO CAPS
      </p>
      <h1 class="font-display mx-auto mt-8 max-w-4xl text-6xl leading-[1.02] sm:text-8xl">
        Your voice,<br /><em class="serif-em">finally</em> heard.
      </h1>
      <p class="mx-auto mt-7 max-w-xl text-lg leading-8 text-ink-dim">
        WhisperFlow turns speech into clean, polished text in any app — transcribed and
        refined entirely on your machine by open models. Free. Unlimited. Un-cloudable.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-3">
        <a href="/whisperflow/download/" class="btn-primary">Get started on Windows</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/namandhakad712/whisperflow" class="btn-ink">Star on GitHub</a>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-5 font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.12em] text-ink-faint">FREE FOREVER · NO ACCOUNT · NO WORD CAPS</p>

      <!-- floating demo — glass over glow, isometric slab behind -->
      <div class="relative mx-auto mt-20 max-w-2xl pb-8">
        <!-- hand-authored isometric slab -->
        <svg class="pointer-events-none absolute -top-16 left-1/2 -translate-x-1/2" width="560" height="300" viewBox="0 0 560 300" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
          <g opacity="0.55">
            <polygon points="280,40 500,130 280,220 60,130" fill="url(#slab)"/>
            <polygon points="280,220 500,130 500,150 280,240" fill="#0B1B4D" opacity="0.8"/>
            <polygon points="280,220 60,130 60,150 280,240" fill="#07123A" opacity="0.9"/>
            <polyline points="180,120 240,95 300,120 360,95" stroke="#4C6FFF" stroke-width="1.5" opacity="0.8"/>
            <polyline points="200,140 260,115 320,140 380,115" stroke="#8FB0FF" stroke-width="1" opacity="0.5"/>
            <circle cx="180" cy="120" r="3" fill="#8FB0FF"/>
            <circle cx="380" cy="115" r="3" fill="#4C6FFF"/>
          </g>
          <defs>
            <linearGradient id="slab" x1="60" y1="40" x2="500" y2="220">
              <stop stop-color="#0B1B4D"/>
              <stop offset="1" stop-color="#07123A"/>
            </linearGradient>
          </defs>
        </svg>
        <div class="glass-panel relative p-2 shadow-[0_0_90px_rgba(41,82,227,0.25)]">
          <div class="rounded-2xl border border-line/70 bg-[#0A0B10]/80 px-6 py-5 text-left backdrop-blur-xl">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
              <span class="font-mono text-[11px] text-ink-dim">Ctrl+Shift+Space</span>
              <span class="flex items-center gap-1.5 font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[0.14em] text-[#8FB0FF]">
                <span class="h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#4C6FFF] shadow-[0_0_8px_rgba(76,111,255,0.9)]"></span> LOCAL
              </span>
            </div>
            <div class="mt-5 flex h-12 items-center justify-center gap-1" aria-hidden="true">
              {[12, 26, 38, 20, 44, 30, 14, 40, 24, 46, 18, 34, 28, 42, 16, 36, 22, 10, 32, 24].map((h, i) => (
                <span
                  class="w-1.5 origin-center rounded-full bg-gradient-to-b from-[#8FB0FF] to-[#2952E3]"
                  style={`height:${h}px;animation:wv 1.1s ease-in-out ${i * 0.06}s infinite`}
                ></span>
              ))}
            </div>
            <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-ink-dim">
              so basically um ship the demo
              <span class="ml-2 rounded-lg bg-[#2952E3]/25 px-2 py-0.5 text-[#DCE6FF]">“So basically, ship the demo.”</span>
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <style>{`@keyframes wv{0%,100%{transform:scaleY(.3)}50%{transform:scaleY(1)}}`}</style>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ================= ORBIT — everything on your machine ================= -->
  <section class="relative mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-28 sm:px-6 sm:py-36">
    <div class="text-center">
      <h2 class="font-display text-4xl leading-tight sm:text-6xl">
        Everything runs <em class="serif-em">here.</em>
      </h2>
      <p class="mx-auto mt-5 max-w-md text-ink-dim">
        Not on a server somewhere. On the machine you already own.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-16 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-3">
      {[
        ["Ear", "whisper.cpp listens", "Streaming transcription with silence detection — 100+ languages, zero audio leaves the device."],
        ["Mind", "llama.cpp polishes", "A small local LLM removes filler, fixes punctuation, follows your tone. Or bring any OpenAI-compatible endpoint."],
        ["Memory", "yours alone", "Dictionary, commands and history live in local storage. One switch makes the app physically unable to phone home."],
      ].map(([tag, title, body]) => (
        <div class="glass-panel group p-7 transition-shadow hover:shadow-[0_0_70px_rgba(41,82,227,0.18)]">
          <p class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[0.18em] text-[#8FB0FF]">{tag.toUpperCase()}</p>
          <h3 class="font-display mt-3 text-2xl italic">{title}</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-ink-dim">{body}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ================= STATS — the meter that stays at zero ================= -->
  <section class="relative mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 pb-28 sm:px-6 sm:pb-36">
    <div class="glass-panel relative overflow-hidden p-10 text-center sm:p-16">
      <div class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 bg-[radial-gradient(600px_240px_at_50%_0%,rgba(41,82,227,0.22),transparent_70%)]" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="relative">
        <h2 class="font-display text-4xl leading-tight sm:text-5xl">
          The only meter is <em class="serif-em">yours</em>.
        </h2>
        <div class="mt-12 grid gap-8 sm:grid-cols-3">
          {[
            ["0", "bytes of audio sent to any cloud"],
            ["~3s", "from hotkey to polished text"],
            ["∞", "words per week. forever."],
          ].map(([big, label]) => (
            <div>
              <p class="font-display text-6xl text-transparent" style="background:linear-gradient(100deg,#8FB0FF,#2952E3);-webkit-background-clip:text;background-clip:text">{big}</p>
              <p class="mt-2 font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[0.16em] text-ink-faint">{label.toUpperCase()}</p>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ================= FAQ ================= -->
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 pb-28 sm:px-6 sm:pb-36">
    <h2 class="font-display text-center text-4xl sm:text-5xl">
      Good <em class="serif-em">questions.</em>
    </h2>
    <div class="mt-12 space-y-3">
      {[
        ["Is it really free?", "Yes — the core app is free forever, with no word caps or accounts. Sponsor tiers fund development; they don't unlock dictation, because dictation isn't locked."],
        ["Does it need the internet?", "Only once, to download models from HuggingFace. After that it works fully offline — planes, airports, hotel Wi-Fi."],
        ["How is this different from cloud dictation?", "Cloud tools stream your voice to servers and meter your words. WhisperFlow transcribes locally with whisper.cpp and polishes locally with a small LLM — private, unlimited, free."],
        ["What hardware does it need?", "Any modern PC. 8 GB RAM runs the balanced setup; 16 GB unlocks the best models. Onboarding checks and recommends for you."],
        ["Windows only?", "Windows ships first; the engine is cross-platform and macOS/Linux packaging is on the roadmap."],
      ].map(([q, a]) => (
        <details class="faq glass-panel group p-6">
          <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-4 text-[15px] font-medium">
            {q}
            <span class="faq-chevron text-xl leading-none text-ink-faint transition-transform">+</span>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-6 text-ink-dim">{a}</p>
        </details>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ================= CTA — hand it the busywork ================= -->
  <section class="void-glow relative overflow-hidden border-t border-line">
    <div class="relative mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-32 text-center sm:px-6 sm:py-40">
      <h2 class="font-display mx-auto max-w-3xl text-5xl leading-[1.05] sm:text-7xl">
        Hand WhisperFlow<br /><em class="serif-em">the talking.</em>
      </h2>
      <p class="mx-auto mt-6 max-w-md text-ink-dim">
        Download, pick a model, dictate your first sentence in under five minutes.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-3">
        <a href="/whisperflow/download/" class="btn-primary">Get started on Windows</a>
        <a href="/whisperflow/features/" class="btn-ink">Explore features</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
